 "notes": "Method paper: no property or biological test in the packet, so the spine stops at STR; PRP/PRF appear only as argued discussion (b35, b38). The argument is design -> mold -> cast -> does the product reproduce the design? That fidelity check is the main multimodal act (proposed mm_op match_to_design on b12, b15, b22). Branches: four scaffold families (biphasic HA/PLA, PLA/PGA, single-polymer global-porous, trabecular, global+local porous) collapsed into shared STR claims with attrs. Image audit: F7C local pores are ~5-35 um vs text 50-100 um (contradicts; the paper's own shrinkage/section-plane excuse is b33); F5A starred 'air-bubble voids' are mostly slit-shaped; F6 shows detached strut fragments against 'interconnectivity apparent'; F4B does not resolve the PGA/PLA interface. F3B and F6 are 3D uCT surface renders (recorded as spatial_map with attrs.proposed_modality=volume_render). Lost: mold shrinkage compensation (1.37x), cement molds, PSA vs wax mold chemistry, RDO etching protocol, circular vs square channel variants. PRC->PRC chaining uses proposed rel feeds_into (b8->b9->b10/b11); if rejected, fall back to premise_for."
